    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine when Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together tutoring in the lab, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of their working intervals. Darren works every third school day, Wanda every fourth school day, Beatrice every sixth school day, and Chi every seventh school day. The LCM of these numbers will give us the number of school days after which all four tutors will be in the lab on the same day.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorizations of the numbers:\n- The prime factorization of 3 is \\(3\\).\n- The prime factorization of 4 is \\(2^2\\).\n- The prime factorization of 6 is \\(2 \\times 3\\).\n- The prime factorization of 7 is \\(7\\).\n\nThe LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in these factorizations. The primes involved are 2, 3, and 7. The highest power of 2 is \\(2^2\\), the highest power of 3 is \\(3\\), and the highest power of 7 is \\(7\\).\n\nTherefore, the LCM is:\n\\[\n2^2 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 4 \\times 3 \\times 7 = 84\n\\]\n\nThis means that Wanda, Darren, Beatrice, and Chi will next be together tutoring in the lab in \\(\\boxed{84}\\) school days.",
